{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "subsection_title", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\subsection{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{subsection-category-prelims}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:335381893b9b7a0877a1029ef758af23311270506b7361dd06964a96f9c79341", "source_text": "Category-theoretic preliminaries", "source_text_hash": "sha256:be3474df0a82efdaa730bbd22ed5e291f276bff01f078a7322efa24ae2eb7d02", "unit_id": "tag:08WF:title"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$g_1, g_2: B \\to C$", "MATH_0002": "$g_1$", "MATH_0003": "$g_2$", "MATH_0004": "$f: A \\to B$", "MATH_0005": "$g_1 \\circ f = g_2 \\circ f$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{A' \\ar[rd]^e \\ar@/^1.5pc/[rrd] \\ar@{-->}[d] & & \\\\\nA \\ar[r]^f & B \\ar@<1ex>[r]^{g_1} \\ar@<-1ex>[r]_{g_2} & \nC\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-equalizer}\n\\xymatrix{\nA \\ar[r]^f  & B \\ar@<1ex>[r]^{g_1} \\ar@<-1ex>[r]_{g_2} & C\n}\n\\end{equation}", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-section-equalizers}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-section-coequalizers}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:970a7dfbe6ab85e5cd1210b1429fa2f78d1980b7a9491ea822eab723562687c7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8b0ac451747cb766a21c585ccabf09f601ba36d09cb08ce369946ebc28f4c277", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe start by recalling a few basic notions from category theory which will \nsimplify the exposition. In this subsection, fix an ambient category.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nFor two morphisms <MATH_0001>, recall that an <TEXTITOPEN_0001>equalizer<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nof <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003>  is a morphism <MATH_0004> which satisfies\n<MATH_0005> and is universal for this property.\nThis second statement means that any commutative diagram \n<MATH_0006>\nwithout the dashed arrow can be uniquely completed. We also say in this \nsituation that the diagram\n<MATH_0007>\nis an equalizer. Reversing arrows gives the definition of a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>coequalizer<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>.\nSee Categories, Sections <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nSince it involves a universal property, the property of being an equalizer is \ntypically not stable under applying a covariant functor. Just as for\nmonomorphisms and epimorphisms, one can get around this in some\ncases by exhibiting splittings.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:83178d21e3d577d92bce54ec3cc8c337c900d56b0a5c4c738da859c34c319695", "unit_id": "tag:08WF:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$g_1 \\circ f = g_2 \\circ f$", "MATH_0002": "$h : B \\to A$", "MATH_0003": "$i : C \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-split-equalizer-conditions}\nh \\circ f = 1_A, \\quad f \\circ h = i \\circ g_1, \\quad i \\circ g_2 = 1_B.\n\\end{equation}", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-equalizer}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-split-equalizer}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:addc919d292a5c5839a7ad1d7d814360639684d99a76b2a00938301959dff5ad", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:92414f690988ad7461a0dfa305b4bdee2d77acd3b39a792856a20bd76971db86", "source_text": "A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>split equalizer<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a diagram (<REF_0001>) with\n<MATH_0001> for which there exist auxiliary morphisms\n<MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> such that\n<MATH_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:19b5aa098f7018acb1d16cedbfa0735a640bda7da84831791b10ce9d06d29704", "unit_id": "tag:08WH:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$e$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$e = f \\circ (h \\circ e)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-equalizer}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:78fa9cf4c2102523f396c6da9e23a3dffb397e8e0f322e3bc0166b27f4b4d9ce", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:278649e0732a8c1354acf7bfddf5afc6b3b021bd5357946923a57606c87f6a8a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe point is that the equalities among arrows force (<REF_0001>) \nto be an equalizer: the map <MATH_0001> factors uniquely through <MATH_0002> by writing\n<MATH_0003>. Consequently, applying a covariant functor\nto a split equalizer gives a split equalizer; applying a contravariant functor \ngives a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>split coequalizer<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, whose definition is apparent.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:944f86361682490e7ad667b6e2e1faaa8e9f83de4639f8f7735f866cd3c024eb", "unit_id": "tag:08WF:prose-0002"}
